column32:
It would be a little more cumbersome to write, but the same effect can be achieved easily:<p><pre><code>  A a = new A();
  try {
      B(a);
      return C(a);
  } finally {
      a.cleanup();
  }
 </code></pre>
Transforms into:<p><pre><code>  Either<Exception, Result> ret;

  A a = new A();

  ret = B(a);
  if (ret.isRight()) ret = C(a);

  a.cleanup();
  return ret;
</code></pre>
Maybe someone can rewrite this even more cleanly. I can think of an easy-to-generate improvement containing a GOTO.
